<title>ARGENTINA: Argentina's Gatic says it now paid bond interest.</title>
<headline>Argentina's Gatic says it now paid bond interest.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina's Gatic, manufacturer of Adidas, New Balance and other sportswear, said Tuesday it has made the interest payments on a $40 million Eurobond that it failed to pay off when it matured Monday.</p>
<p>Salvador Ritaca, spokesman for the company, said in a press release the interest had now been paid.</p>
<p>Ritaca said negotiations to restructure the bond with the original underwriters of the three-year issue, Britain's Standard Chartered and local Banco Comafi, were making headway.</p>
</text>
